    "3": {
      "outcome": "correct",
      "finding": "The defining substance is dental pathology, diagnosis, prevention and treatment, delivered through sustained dental knowledge, phantom-head/preclinical procedures and supervised patient clinics. UCR has genuine general anatomy, physiology, biochemistry, infection, pharmacology, molecular pathology and biomedical laboratory study, and genuine psychology, ethics, communication and organisation. These study related bodily or social processes but do not provide oral/dental anatomy, cariology, periodontology, endodontics, dental materials/restoration, radiology competencies or supervised dental treatment. Neither full proposed curriculum substantively develops that defining dental sequence. The biomedical option remains general biomedicine; the patient-care option remains general psychology/leadership/communication. No adjacent course is a substitute for missing dentistry. Both alternatives withdrawn.",
